{"key": "Medical::Medical-97625b74", "time": "2026-10-09T15:23:22+00:00", "raw": {"candidates": [{"content": {"role": "model", "parts": [{"text": "Main diagnostic methods for breast cancer include physical exams, imaging tests such as diagnostic mammograms, ultrasound, MRI, and PET-CT scans, as well as blood tests. Diagnosis is confirmed through biopsies, including fine-needle aspiration, core needle biopsy, vacuum-assisted core biopsy, incisional biopsy, excisional biopsy, skin biopsy, and axillary lymph node biopsy, followed by laboratory analysis for hormone receptors and HER2 status. Common breast cancer symptoms include a breast lump, pain, nipple thickening or discharge, and changes in the shape or size of the breast. In subtypes such as inflammatory breast cancer, common signs and symptoms include a swollen and red breast that feels warm to the touch, skin thickening, pitted or dimpled skin resembling an orange peel, edema, and erythema.", "thoughtSignature": ""}]}, "finishReason": "STOP", "groundingMetadata": {"groundingChunks": [{"retrievedContext": {"uri": "Medical.txt", "title": "Medical.txt"}}, {"retrievedContext": {"uri": "Medical.txt", "title": "Medical.txt"}}, {"retrievedContext": {"uri": "Medical.txt", "title": "Medical.txt"}}, {"retrievedContext": {"uri": "Medical.txt", "title": "Medical.txt"}}], "groundingSupports": [{"segment": {"endIndex": 168, "text": "Main diagnostic methods for breast cancer include physical exams, imaging tests such as diagnostic mammograms, ultrasound, MRI, and PET-CT scans, as well as blood tests"}, "groundingChunkIndices": [0, 1, 2]}, {"segment": {"startIndex": 170, "endIndex": 446, "text": "Diagnosis is confirmed through biopsies, including fine-needle aspiration, core needle biopsy, vacuum-assisted core biopsy, incisional biopsy, excisional biopsy, skin biopsy, and axillary lymph node biopsy, followed by laboratory analysis for hormone receptors and HER2 status"}, "groundingChunkIndices": [1, 2]}, {"segment": {"startInde